The attached image, Figure 4, illustrates the enhanced uptake of antigens by bone marrow-derived dendritic cells (BMDCs) when formulated with Nano-11 nanoparticles. Confocal microscopy shows that soluble FITC-labeled ovalbumin (OVA) alone (middle row) is poorly internalized by BMDCs. In contrast, AF647-labeled Nano-11 nanoparticles (top row) are efficiently phagocytized. When OVA is adsorbed to Nano-11 (bottom row), there is a significant increase in OVA uptake by BMDCs, with both Nano-11 and OVA co-localizing within the cells, indicating that Nano-11 effectively delivers antigens intracellularly and remains associated with them.